{"id":"nb444247e9c","headline":"Energy bill cap 'won't go up in October' but you will pay much more","summary":"The energy bill cap will not go up in October, but households will still pay much more. The news comes ahead of a large jump in gas and electricity bills expected this week.","why":"The UK energy price cap sets the maximum unit rates suppliers can charge households, linking retail energy costs to wholesale gas and power prices. Changes affect inflation and consumer spending.","category":"economy","event_type":"regulation","importance":2,"flag":null,"market_moving":false,"location":{"place":"London","country":"United Kingdom","lat":51.5,"lon":-0.12,"region":"eu"},"entities":[],"links":[],"source":{"name":"Wales Online","url":"https://www.walesonline.co.uk/news/uk-news/energy-bill-cap-wont-go-34201959"},"sources":[{"name":"Wales Online","url":"https://www.walesonline.co.uk/news/uk-news/energy-bill-cap-wont-go-34201959"}],"published_at":"2026-06-29T05:20:44Z","retrieved_at":"2026-11-17T13:38:59Z","official":false,"ai_summary":true,"content_hash":"a222913afc814192","impacts":[],"why_moved":null,"backfilled":true,"backfilled_at":"2026-11-17T13:38:59Z","backfill_provenance":{"version":"gdelt-backfill-v1","original_published_at":"2026-06-29T05:20:44Z","feed_url":"https://data.gdeltproject.org/gdeltv2/","discovered_via":"GDELT GKG 2.1","gdelt_seen":"2026-06-29T06:00:00Z","publisher_country_gdelt":"IS","description_from":"publisher page metadata"},"image":{"kind":"topic","file":"photos/gas-pipeline-1898766.jpg","alt":"gas pipeline (illustration)","credit":"Brida_staright","license":"Pixabay Content License","license_url":"https://pixabay.com/service/license-summary/","source":"Pixabay","source_url":"https://pixabay.com/photos/pipe-line-house-iron-pipes-1898766/"}}